    "display_name": "Simulating an Outbreak",
    "long_instructions": "**An outbreak of a disease, such as a virus, can spread by multiplying—much like the viral social media post you saw in class.**\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n- Complete `simulate` to simulate a virus spreading over any number of days.\r\n- Ensure that, for each day, `simulate` prints a message in the format: `\"Day {day}: {infections} infections\"`. Start with day 0.\r\n- Choose the starting conditions for your virus and call `simulate`.\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nRemember that Python’s `for` loop can repeat code a certain number of times. For example:\r\n\r\n```\r\niterations = 10\r\nfor i in range(iterations):\r\n    print(i)\r\n```",
